column202:
10/Sep/26 12:24 PM;eraymond;I have created a webserver ssw-phc-s7-vm-nginx.cwsdeveng.com which can act as a centralized webserver and allow all vm's with web applications to use the webserver url with the application name appended at the end of the url to access the specified application. This allows one corticate to be used from the webserver using tls termination at the proxy, or we could do TLS end to end and then we would need to store each servers certificate on the webserver, it is not too much more work to do that, just need to renew the servers certificates from time to time just as we would for the webserver where if we just tls termination at the proxy on the web server we only need to worry about renewing the webserver certificate from time to time. 

I need some apps to test this out on to see how they behave but all indications is the webserver is running and configured properly. The test page is accessible from mulitple VM's through https.

Also during setup I ran into issues again with the gold image affecting my enrollment to the IDM server for the new Hostname and IP address. I do feel that we should recreate the gold image so that it is not enrolled in the IDM and we can easily enroll the new VM's created from the clones without running into issues where we need to purge artifacts of the gold image. ;;;

